* ------------------------------------------------------- observation nodes
Bvdiff VDIFF 0 V = V(OUTP) - V(OUTN)
Bvcm   VCM   0 V = (V(OUTP) + V(OUTN))/2 - @@VDD_NOM@@
Bvtail VTL   0 V = V(TAIL)
Rvdiff VDIFF 0 1G
Rvcm   VCM   0 1G
Rvtail VTL   0 1G

.ic v(OUTP)=@@IC_OUTP@@ v(OUTN)=@@IC_OUTN@@

.control
* pre_osdi must come before the first analysis command: ngspice defers OSDI
* instantiation to analysis setup, so a `pre_osdi` issued later leaves the 32
* sg13_hv_svaricap instances unresolved. sim/tools/build-osdi.sh builds this
* binary; osc_bench.sh calls it, so a cold checkout needs no manual step.
pre_osdi @@OSDI_MOSVAR@@
* The netlist's own `.save i(vsup)` is stripped (see above). This `save` names
* the ten vectors the extractors and the operating-point print actually read.
* It is NOT `save all`: `save all` additionally stores every internal node of
* the 32 varactor subcircuits, the two inductor ladders and the four HBTs at
* every accepted timepoint, which measured 169 s against 153 s for this same
* 2 ns transient (~10 % of the run) while producing a bit-identical extracted
* f_osc and Vpp. Naming the set is the cheaper and the more explicit of the
* two. It must stay in sync with the wrdata/print lines below -- a vector that
* is read but not saved comes back empty, and osc_simulate_point records that
* point as a FAIL rather than silently reporting a zero.
save v(VDIFF) v(VCM) v(VTL) i(VSUP) v(NBIAS) v(TE) v(RE) v(TAIL) v(OUTP) v(OUTN)
alter VCT dc = @@VCTRL@@
op
* The DC operating point, printed so the record can report the SMALL-SIGNAL
* supply current separately from the large-signal one. Row 8 is the
* large-signal number -- the pair's average current shifts once it is
* switching -- but reporting only one of the two would hide which is which.
echo op_point_follows
print v(NBIAS) v(TE) v(RE) v(TAIL) v(OUTP) v(OUTN) i(VSUP)
tran @@TSTEP@@ @@TSTOP@@ 0 @@TMAX@@
let vdiff_w = v(VDIFF)
wrdata @@OUT_PREFIX@@_vdiff vdiff_w
let vcm_w = v(VCM)
wrdata @@OUT_PREFIX@@_vcm vcm_w
let vtail_w = v(VTL)
wrdata @@OUT_PREFIX@@_vtail vtail_w
* Sign flipped so the recorded number is current OUT of the rail.
let isup_w = -i(VSUP)
wrdata @@OUT_PREFIX@@_isup isup_w
.endc
.end
